-- RelicOpening: the salvage opening, a summon-style show played in the world on the player's own
-- camera. It is the whole reveal for salvages (RevealController no longer shows its card after
-- it). Designed with the roblox-vfx skill's method (stylised_game style; beats: a rarity-tease
-- escalation, suck-in + dark beat before the release, a hard 1-2 frame white flash with a colour
-- swap to the rarity hue). Reference: docs/reference/chest_opening (Round 6).
--
--   RelicOpening.Play(relic, { onDone = fn, play = fn(soundName, pitch)? })
--
-- The camera stays the player's own (no CameraType change, owner feedback 2026-11-16). The chest
-- is placed relative to the camera every frame (stageTarget: big, centred, at eye level, facing
-- the camera, its top tilted a little towards it), so it reads like a summon pad whatever the
-- player does. The world behind it is blurred (DepthOfField focused on the chest), the HUD is
-- hidden, and the diver is hidden if they would stand between the camera and the chest.
--
-- Timeline (scaled by rarity tier 1..7):
--   DROP     the chest drops in and lands with a dust puff; blur and a dim, desaturated grade
--   TEASE    one step per tier: the lid seam glows the next rarity's colour, the chest hops, a
--            rarity word pops (COMMON... UNCOMMON!... RARE!!). Shaking, light leaks and sparks grow
--            with the tension; steps come faster and faster
--   RELEASE  suck-in (squash) + dark beat, then a 1-2 frame white flash, FOV punch and shake; the
--            lid blasts off spinning, the chest shrinks away; burst layers in the rarity colour;
--            letterbox + tinted whiteout for Legendary+
--   REVEAL   the relic pops out where the chest was, inside a rarity-coloured bubble flash, with
--            big sparkle stars at the screen edges
--   HOLD     a rarity god-ray backdrop turns behind the relic and the FOV pushes in slowly. Text:
--            the name on top (outlined, a thin line with diamond ends), the rarity word in its
--            colour, material / mutation / income chips, and "(Click anywhere to continue)".
--            Nothing auto-closes: a click, tap, gamepad A or Enter ends it.
-- Tap during the tease to skip to the release. Everything is local and cleaned up afterwards.
--
-- Effects: our own layers with textures generated by the roblox-vfx skill (TEX): ring pulses,
-- comic pops behind the words, a magic circle under the chest, a charge-in, a shockwave, focus
-- lines, a lens streak, streak sparks, stars, a fireball, landing dust, embers and glitter, plus
-- confetti. (This was "version B" of an A/B test; the owner picked it and the LihFolk version A
-- was removed on 2026-11-16.)

